    "id": "med_38",
    "name_en": "Alcaftadine",
    "generic": "Alcaftadine",
    "category": "ophthalmic",
    "category_bn": "চোখ ও অপথ্যালমোলজি",
    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Prevention of itching associated with allergic conjunctivitis)",
    "primary_indication": "Prevention of itching associated with allergic conjunctivitis",
    "indications": "Alcaftadine eye drops is indicated for the prevention of itching associated with allergic conjunctivitis. Alcaftadine ophthalmic solution is an H1 receptor antagonist, in a sterile ophthalmic solution for to pical ophthalmic use.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "This eye drops is a sterile to pical ophthalmic solution containing Alcaftadine. Alcaftadine is an histamine receptor antagonist and inhibitor of the release of histamine from mast cell. It is also a potent histamine H2 and H4 receptor antagonist that has demonstrated anti-inflammatory property. In doing so, antihistaminic effect provides relief from itching associated with early phase of ocular allergic response, whereas mast cell stabilization inhibits the release of mediators such as cytokines and lipid mediators that play a role in late-phase response of allergic conjunctivitis.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adults and children 2 years and over: Instill one drop in each eye once daily.",
    "side_effects_bn": "The most frequent ocular reactions are eye irritation, burning or/and stinging upon instillation, eye redness and eye pruritus, nasopharyngitis and headache.",
    "precautions_bn": "To minimize eye injury and contamination of the dropper tip and solution, care should be taken not to to uch the eyelids or surrounding areas with the dropper tip of the bottle. Patients should be advised not to wear a contact lens if their eye is red. This preparation should not be used to treat contact lens related irritation and should not be instilled while wearing contact lenses. Remove contact lenses prior to instillation this preparation. Lenses may be reinserted after 10 minutes following administration. If more than 1 to pical ophthalmic medicinal product is being used, each one should be administered at least 5 minutes apart.",
