    "target_organ": "Heart / হৃৎপিণ্ড ও রক্ত সংবহনতন্ত্র",
    "organ_key": "heart",
    "work_bn": "উচ্চ রক্তচাপ নিয়ন্ত্রণ, হৃদযন্ত্রে রক্ত সঞ্চালন স্বাভাবিক রাখা এবং হার্ট অ্যাটাক ও এনজাইনা বুকের ব্যথা প্রতিরোধে কার্যকর। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Skin moisturization)",
    "primary_indication": "Skin moisturization",
    "indications": "It is indicated for Co-enzyme Q10 deficiency and mitochondrial disorders. It is also used in congestive heart failure, myocardial infarction, high blood pressure (hypertension) in combination with other medications, preventing migraine headache, parkinson's disease, improving the immune system, infertility in men and muscular dystrophy.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Co-enzyme Q10 is a vitamin-like substance found throughout the body especially in the heart, liver, kidney and pancreas. It is required for the proper function of many organs and chemical reactions in the body. It helps to provide energy to cells. It has antioxidant activity.",
    "dosage_bn": "For Co-enzyme Q10 deficiency: 150 mg daily. For mitochondrial disorders: 150-160 mg, or 2 mg/kg/day. For heart failure in adults: 100 mg per day divided into 2 or 3 doses. For recent myocardial infarction: 120 mg daily in 2 divided doses. For high blood pressure: 120-200 mg per day divided into 2 doses. For isolated systolic hypertension: 60 mg twice daily. For preventing migraine headache: 100 mg three times daily. For Parkinson's disease: 300 mg, 600 mg, 1200 mg and 2400 mg per day in 3-4 divided doses. For infertility in men: 200-300 mg per day. For muscular dystrophy: 100 mg per day. Dividing the to tal daily dose by taking smaller amounts two or three times a day instead of a large amount all at once can help to reduce side effects.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Co-enzyme Q10 is safe for most adults. It can cause some mild side effects including stomach upset, loss of appetite, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. It can cause allergic skin rashes in some people.",
    "precautions_bn": "Co-enzyme Q10 may lower blood sugar levels, so caution should be taken in patients with diabetes or hypoglycemia. Co-enzyme Q10 may decrease blood pressure so caution is advised in patients with low blood pressure or taking blood pressure medications.",
