    "name_en": "Bacitracin Zinc + Polymyxin B Sulfate",
    "generic": "Bacitracin Zinc + Polymyxin B Sulfate",
    "category": "ophthalmic",
    "category_bn": "চোখ ও অপথ্যালমোলজি",
    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Diaper rash)",
    "primary_indication": "Diaper rash",
    "indications": "This ophthalmic ointment is indicated in the treatment of bacterial infections of the eye and its adnexa including conjunctivitis, keratitis, corneal ulceration and ulcerative blepharitis. It may be applied to prevent ocular infection both pre and post operatively.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "This ophthalmic ointment is a sterile antimicrobial ointment for ophthalmic use, cointaining Polymixin-B sulphate and Bacitracin Zinc. Polymixin-B sulphate and Becitracin Zinc are both bactericidal antibiotics, The former exerts its action by binding with the cellular membrane and the later by inhibiting bacterial cell wall development.",
    "dosage_bn": "Apply the ointment every 3 to 4 hourly for 7 to 10 days, depending on the severity of the infection or as directed by the physician.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Sometimes this ointment may be absorbed in the blood, but shows no blood related to xicity. Moreover Allergic reaction, eye irritation, eye redness, itching, swelling may occur.",
    "precautions_bn": "Polytracin is contraindicated in those individuals who have shown hypersensitivity to Polymixin-B sulphate, Becitracin Zinc or to cross sensitizing substances.",
    "pregnancy_category": "C",
