    "id": "med_378",
    "name_en": "Candesartan Cilexetil + Hydrochlorothiazide",
    "generic": "Candesartan Cilexetil + Hydrochlorothiazide",
    "category": "cardio",
    "category_bn": "হৃদরোগ ও রক্তচাপ",
    "icon": "❤️",
    "target_organ": "Heart / হৃৎপিণ্ড ও রক্ত সংবহনতন্ত্র",
    "organ_key": "heart",
    "work_bn": "উচ্চ রক্তচাপ নিয়ন্ত্রণ, হৃদযন্ত্রে রক্ত সঞ্চালন স্বাভাবিক রাখা এবং হার্ট অ্যাটাক ও এনজাইনা বুকের ব্যথা প্রতিরোধে কার্যকর। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Hypertension)",
    "primary_indication": "Hypertension",
    "indications": "This is indicated for the treatment of hypertension, congestive heart failure.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Candesartan Cilexetil-Hydrochlorothiazide combines an angiotensin II receptor blocker, Candesartan Cilexetil and a diuretic, Hydrochlorothiazide. Candesartan Cilexetil is an ester prodrug that is hydrolysed in the body to the active form Candesartan during absorption from the gastrointestinal tract. Candesartan blocks the vasoconstrictor and aldosterone-secreting effects of angiotensin II by selectively blocking the binding of angiotensin II to the AT1 receptor in many tissues (eg, vascular smooth muscle, adrenal gland). Hydrochlorothiazide is a thiazide diuretic. Thiazides affect the renal tubular mechanisms of electrolyte reabsorption, directly by increasing sodium excreation. Indirectly, the diuretic action of hydrochlorothiazide reduces plasma volume with consequent increase in plasma renin activity, aldosterone secretion, urinary potassium loss, and decrease in serum potassium. The renin-aldosterone link is mediated by angiotensin II, so coadministration of Candesartan tends to reverse the potassium loss associated with Hydrochlorothiazide.",
    "dosage_bn": "The usual dose is one tablet once daily.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Mild and transient in nature. The overall incidence of adverse events is comparable to placebo. Side effects are headache, upper respiratory tract infection, back pain, influenza-like symptoms.",
    "precautions_bn": "No patient receiving this combination was discontinued due to increases or decreases in serum potassium. Overall, the combination of candesartan cilexetil and hydrochlorothiazide had no clinically significant effect on serum potassium.",
    "pregnancy_category": "D",
    "brands": "Giran H, Giran-H",
    "brand_list": [
      "Giran H",
      "Giran-H"
    ],
    "manufacturers": [
      "Aristopharma Limited",
      "Aristopharma Ltd."
    ],
    "dosage_forms": [
      "Tablet"
    ],
    "strengths": [
      "8 mg+12.5 mg"
    ],
    "therapeutic_class": "Combined antihypertensive preparations"
