    "target_organ": "Kidneys & Bladder / কিডনি ও মূত্রথলি",
    "organ_key": "kidneys",
    "work_bn": "কিডনি ও মূত্রথলির কার্যক্ষমতা রক্ষা, প্রস্রাবের স্বাভাবিক প্রবাহ নিশ্চিতকরণ এবং প্রোস্টেট উপসর্গ নিরাময়ে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Prostate carcinoma)",
    "primary_indication": "Prostate carcinoma",
    "indications": "Prevention of skeletal related events (pathological fracture, radiation to bone, spinal cord compression or bone surgery) in patients with bone metastases from solid tumours.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Denosumab binds to Receptor activator of nuclear factor kappa-B ligand (RANKL), a transmembrane or soluble protein essential for the formation, function, and survival of osteoclasts, the cells responsible for bone resorption. Denosumab prevents RANKL from activating its receptor, RANK, on the surface of osteoclasts and their precursors. Prevention of the RANKL/RANK interaction inhibits osteoclast formation, function, and survival, thereby decreasing bone resorption and increasing bone mass and strength in both cortical and trabecular bone.",
    "dosage_bn": "Subcutaneous Injection: 120 mg once every 4 wk into thigh, abdomen or upper arm. Ca & vitamin D supplements should be given whilst undergoing treatment.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Dyspnoea, Hypocalcaemia, hypophosphataemia, Osteonecrosis of the Jaw (ONJ).",
    "precautions_bn": "Correct preexisting hypocalcaemia prior to therapy. Osteonecrosis of the jaw (ONJ). Perform oral & dental exam with preventive dentistry prior to treatment. Avoid invasive dental procedures & maintain good oral hygiene while on treatment. Atypical femoral fractures. Severe renal impairment (CrCl <30 ml/min) or in patients receiving dialysis. Concomitant use with other denosumab-containing prep. Pregnancy & lactation. Children.",
