    "work_bn": "শারীরিক অসুস্থতা উপশম ও রোগীর দ্রুত আরোগ্যের জন্য চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শে নির্দেশিত।",
    "primary_indication": "",
    "indications": "Deferiprone is indicated for the treatment of iron overload patients with thalassemia major when deferoxamine therapy is contraindicated or inadequate. Deferiprone therapy should be initiated and maintained by a physician experienced in the treatment of patients with thalassemia.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Deferiprone is a chelating agent with an affinity for ferric ion (iron III). Deferiprone binds with ferric ions to form neutral 3:1 (deferiprone:iron) complexes that are stable over a wide range of pH values. Deferiprone has a lower binding affinity for other metals such as copper, aluminum and zinc than for iron.",
    "dosage_bn": "In adults and children over 6 years: this medicine may be given by mouth in doses of 25mg/kg three times daily. Doses above 100mg/kg daily are not recommended. Or, as directed by the registered physician.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Gastrointestinal disorders such as diarrhoea, nausea, vomiting and abdominal pain are common during deferiprone treatment and may require temporary reduction in dose. A reddish brown discoloration of the urine is also common. Other adverse effects that have been reported include arthralgia and increased liver enzymes.",
    "precautions_bn": "Deferiprone has been shown to cause neutropenia including agranulocytosis. The patients neutrophil count should be monitored every week. Caution is advised in patients with hepatic or renal impairment.",
    "pregnancy_category": "D",
