    "organ_key": "lungs",
    "work_bn": "শ্বাসনালী উন্মুক্ত রাখা, কাশি উপশম, ফুসফুসের প্রদাহ রোধ এবং হাঁপানি বা শ্বাসকষ্টের সমস্যা প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Non-productive cough)",
    "primary_indication": "Non-productive cough",
    "indications": "Dextromethorphan is indicated in Chronic dry cough or unproductive cough; Acute dry cough which is interfering with normal function or sleep.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Dextromethorphan suppresses the cough reflex by a direct action on the cough center in the medulla of the brain. Dextromethorphan shows high affinity binding to several regions of the brain, including the medullary cough center. This compound is an NMDA receptor antagonist and acts as a non-competitive channel blocker. It is one of the widely used antitussives, and is also used to study the involvement of glutamate receptors in neurotoxicity.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adults and Children over 12 years: 15 to 30 mg three to four times per day. However, 60 mg doses up to four times per day have been used without increased side effects. Children between 6 and 12 years: 5-15 mg up to four times per day. Children between 2 and 6 years: 2.5-5 mg up to four times per day.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Adverse effects with Dextromethorphan are rare, but nausea and dizziness sometimes occur. The drug produces no analgesia or addiction and little or no CNS depression. Excitation, confusion and respiratory depression may occur after overdosage.",
    "precautions_bn": "Do not use Dextromethorphan to control a cough that is associated with smoking, asthma, or emphysema, or a cough that is productive (produces sputum or phlegm).",
