    "icon": "🫁",
    "target_organ": "Lungs / ফুসফুস ও শ্বাসতন্ত্র",
    "organ_key": "lungs",
    "work_bn": "শ্বাসনালী উন্মুক্ত রাখা, কাশি উপশম, ফুসফুসের প্রদাহ রোধ এবং হাঁপানি বা শ্বাসকষ্টের সমস্যা প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Urticaria)",
    "primary_indication": "Urticaria",
    "indications": "Ebastine is indicated for the symptomatic treatment of: • Seasonal and Perennial Allergic Rhinitis. • Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Ebastine is a long-acting and selective H1-histamine receptor antagonist. After repeated administration, inhibition of peripheral receptors remains at a constant level. Ebastine is rapidly absorbed and undergoes extensive first-pass metabolism following oral administration. Ebastine is almost to tally converted to the pharmacologically active acid metabolite, carebastine.",
    "dosage_bn": "Tablet: • Adults (more than 12 years of age): 10 mg (one tablet) once daily. • Children (6-12 years of age): 5 mg (half tablet) once daily. Syrup: • Children (2-5 years of age): 2.5 ml once daily (upto 5 ml in severe cases such as Perennial Allergic Rhinitis). • Children (6-12 years of age): 5 ml once daily (upto 10 ml in severe cases such as Perennial Allergic Rhinitis). Ebastine may be taken with or without food.",
    "side_effects_bn": "The most common side-effects are headache, dry mouth and drowsiness. Less commonly reported side effects include abdominal pain, dyspepsia, nausea and insomnia.",
    "precautions_bn": "Caution is advised when used in hepatic impairment, renal insufficiency, QTc interval prolongation. Pregnancy, lactation.",
