    "target_organ": "Immune System / রোগপ্রতিরোধ ব্যবস্থা",
    "organ_key": "blood_immune",
    "work_bn": "শরীরের অভ্যন্তরীণ বা বাহ্যিক ক্ষতিকর ব্যাকটেরিয়াজনিত জীবাণু ধ্বংস ও মারাত্মক সংক্রমণ প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত অ্যান্টিবায়োটিক। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Vulvovaginal candidiasis)",
    "primary_indication": "Vulvovaginal candidiasis",
    "indications": "Fenticonazole Nitrate is used for the treatment of vulvovaginal candidiasis.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Fenticonazole is a broad-spectrum antimycotic agent with activity against dermatophytes and yeasts. Fenticonazole has also been shown to exhibit antibacterial action, with a spectrum of activity that includes bacteria commonly associated with vaginal infections and antiparasitic action against the protozoan Trichomonas vaginalis. Therefore, Fenticonazole may be an ideal to pical alternative to multi-agent treatment of mixed infections involving mycotic, bacterial, dermatophyte and/or Trichomonas spp.",
    "dosage_bn": "Route of application is intravaginal. For adults, one applicator full (about 5 gm) is to be administered into the vagina in the morning and evening for three days. After each application, clean it carefully with warm water and soap. Do not use water which is hotter than 50°C or solvents. Then wipe the applicator and store in its packet. Always wash your hands with mild soap and warm water afterwards. Fenticonazole is not greasy and can easily be removed with water.",
    "side_effects_bn": "After intravaginal administration, slight transient burning may occasionally occur, which usually disappears rapidly.",
    "precautions_bn": "It should not be used in conjunction with barrier contraceptives. In the event of a hypersensitivity reaction or development of resistant organisms, treatment should be discontinued and take physician consultation.",
