    "how_it_works_bn": "Glycerin is a hyperosmotic laxative, given rectally, which usually produces a bowel movement within 15 minutes to 1 hour. Hyperosmotic laxatives encourage bowel movements by drawing water into the bowel from surrounding tissues. This produces a softer stool mass and increases bowel action. These products are used for fast, predictable relief of occasional constipation.",
    "dosage_bn": "Children under 2 years: As directed by the physician. Children (2 to 6 years): Only 1 Glycerin 1.15 Suppository per day or as directed by the physician. Adults and Children (From 6 years): Only 1 Glycerin 2.30 Suppository per day or as directed by the physician Insert suppository well up into the rectum. Suppository does not need to melt completely to produce laxative action.",
