    "id": "med_916",
    "name_en": "Ipratropium Bromide (Nebuliser Solution)",
    "generic": "Ipratropium Bromide (Nebuliser Solution)",
    "category": "respiratory",
    "category_bn": "শ্বাসতন্ত্র ও হাঁপানি",
    "icon": "🫁",
    "target_organ": "Lungs / ফুসফুস ও শ্বাসতন্ত্র",
    "organ_key": "lungs",
    "work_bn": "শ্বাসনালী উন্মুক্ত রাখা, কাশি উপশম, ফুসফুসের প্রদাহ রোধ এবং হাঁপানি বা শ্বাসকষ্টের সমস্যা প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Severe bronchospasm)",
    "primary_indication": "Severe bronchospasm",
    "indications": "Ipratropium Nebuliser Solution is indicated as a bronchodilator for maintenance treatment of bronchospasm associated with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, including chronic bronchitis and emphysema.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Ipratropium Bromide is a quaternary ammonium compound with anticholinergic properties. It appears to inhibit vagal reflexes by antagonising the action of acetylcholine (the transmitter agent released from the vagus nerve). Anticholinergics prevent the increase in intracellular concentration of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cyclic GMP) caused by interaction of acetylcholine with the muscarinic receptor on bronchial smooth muscle.",
    "dosage_bn": "Children over 3 years: The usual dose is 0.4-2.0 ml Ipratropium Bromide Solution (100-500 micrograms) up to three times daily. Adults (including elderly and adolescents) over 12 years of age: The usual dose is 0.4-2.0 ml Ipratropium Bromide Solution (100-500 micrograms) up to four times daily.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Allergic-type reactions such as skin rash, angio-oedema of the to ngue, lips and face, urticaria (including giant urticaria), laryngospasm and anaphylactic reactions have been reported, with positive rechallenge in some cases.",
    "precautions_bn": "Ipratropium Bromide should be used with caution in patients predisposed to narrow-angle glaucoma, or with prostatic hyperplasia or bladder-neck obstruction.",
    "pregnancy_category": "",
    "brands": "G-Ipra, Ipramid, Ipratop, Iprex, Rinase",
