    "id": "med_943",
    "name_en": "Irrigating Solution",
    "generic": "Irrigating Solution",
    "category": "ophthalmic",
    "category_bn": "চোখ ও অপথ্যালমোলজি",
    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Removal of foreign bodies)",
    "primary_indication": "Removal of foreign bodies",
    "indications": "Eye Relief removes loose foreign material, air pollutants (smog or pollen), chlorinated water for washing the eye to relieve irritation, stinging, discomfort, itching, burning",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Eye Relief, eye irrigating solution for eye wash can be used for daily or emergency eye cleansing. Boric Acid has mild antibiotic properties against fungal or bacterial infection. Boric Acid is used in eye wash to cleanse or irrigate the eyes. Boric Acid provides soothing relief from eye irritation, and helps remove pollutants from the eye such as smog, chlorine, or other chemicals",
    "dosage_bn": "Instill in the affected eyes as needed or prescribed by the physician. Using without Eye Cup • Flush the affected eye(s) as needed • Control the rate of flow of solution by pressure on the bottle • Do not to uch dropper tip to eye Using with Eye Cup • Fill the cup upto the 5 ml round mark with Eye Relief eye wash solution and apply the cup to the affected eye(s), pressing tightly to prevent leakage • Tilt the head backward. Open eyelids wide and rotate eyeball to wash the eye throughly • Rinse cup with clean water after each use • Close the cap after use",
    "side_effects_bn": "চিকিৎসকের নির্দেশিত সঠিক মাত্রায় পার্শ্বপ্রতিক্রিয়া বিরল। কোনো জটিলতা দেখা দিলে দ্রুত চিকিৎসকের শরণাপন্ন হোন।",
    "precautions_bn": "• Do not use if you have open wounds in or near the eyes, and get medical help right away • Do not use if solution changes color or becomes cloudy • Remove contact lenses before using • Do not to uch tip of container to any surface to avoid contamination • Replace cap after use • Stop use and ask a doctor if you experience eye pain, changes in vision, continued redness or irritation of the eye • Condition worsens or persists • If swallowed, get medical help or contact a Poison Control Center right away.",
