    "work_bn": "হজম প্রক্রিয়া স্বাভাবিক রাখা, পেটে গ্যাস বা মোচড় দূর করা এবং অন্ত্রের সংক্রমণ বা প্রদাহ উপশমে কার্যকর।",
    "primary_indication": "",
    "indications": "Prevention of symptoms of lactose intolerance- • Infantile colic • Abdominal pain • Bloating • Flatulence • Diarrhea • Borborygmi",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Lactase is an enzyme that helps to prevent symptoms of lactose intolerance by breaking down milk sugar (lactose) to produce glucose and galactose via hydrolysis and making dairy foods easier to digest.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: 1 tablet (300 mg) with dairy food. If needed dose can be adjusted up to 2 tablets (600 mg) at a time. Infants: Add lactase enzyme to breast milk or formula in the following directions- Breast Milk: • Express a few tablespoons (2-3 tablespoons) of breast milk into sterilized container • Add 4 drops of lactase paediatric drops • Give mixture to infant on a spoon or oral syringe before initiating breastfeeding • Breast feed as normal Formula: • Add 4 drops of lactase paediatric drops to warm (not hot) formula • Wait 30 minutes, shaking formula occasionally Making formula in advance: • Add 2 drops of lactase paediatric drops to warm formula • Store in refrigerator for minimum 4 hours • Feed Infant as normal • Use within 12 hour • Discard any unused formula Children: Effective & safe in children above 4 years of age.",
    "side_effects_bn": "There are no major side effects reported. The very few side effects may include rash, difficulty in breathing, tightness in chest etc.",
    "precautions_bn": "Some products may contain aspartame and should be avoided in patients with phenylketonuria.\\n\\nHas not been evaluated by the FDA, but is generally recognized as safe (GRAS) for human consumption.",
