    "id": "med_1016",
    "name_en": "Lifitegrast",
    "generic": "Lifitegrast",
    "category": "ophthalmic",
    "category_bn": "চোখ ও অপথ্যালমোলজি",
    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Dry eye)",
    "primary_indication": "Dry eye",
    "indications": "Lifitegrast 5% ophthalmic solution is indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of dry eye disease (DED).",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Lifitegrast binds to the integrin LFA-1, a cell surface protein found on leukocytes and blocks the interaction of LFA-1 with its cognate ligand intercellular adhesion molecule-1 (ICAM-1). ICAM-1 may be overexpressed in corneal and conjunctival tissues in DED. LFA-1/ICAM-1 interaction can contribute to the formation of an immunological synapse resulting in T-cell activation and migration to target tissues. In vitro studies demonstrated that lifitegrast may inhibit Tcell adhesion to ICAM-1 in a human T-cell line and may inhibit secretion of inflammatory cytokines in human peripheral blood mononuclear cells. The exact mechanism of action of lifitegrast in DED is not known.",
    "dosage_bn": "Instill one drop of Lifitegrast twice daily (approximately 12 hours apart) into each eye. Contact lenses should be removed prior to the administration of Lifitegrast and may be reinserted 15 minutes following administration.",
    "side_effects_bn": "The common adverse effects are instillation site irritation, dysgeusia and reduced visual acuity. Less common are blurred vision, conjunctival hyperemia, headache, increased lacrimation, eye discharge, eye discomfort, eye pruritus and sinusitis.",
    "precautions_bn": "Do not to uch the dropper tip to surfaces since this may contaminate the solution. After one month of the opening do not use the medicine of dropper.",
