    "id": "med_1175",
    "name_en": "Nefopam Hydrochloride",
    "generic": "Nefopam Hydrochloride",
    "category": "analgesic",
    "category_bn": "ব্যথানাশক ও অস্থিসন্ধি",
    "icon": "🩹",
    "target_organ": "Bones & Spine / কঙ্কাল ও মেরুদণ্ড",
    "organ_key": "bones_joints",
    "work_bn": "তীব্র শারীরিক ব্যথা, অস্থিসন্ধি ও মেরুদণ্ডের প্রদাহ, বাত এবং জ্বর দ্রুত উপশম করতে সহায়ক। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Pain)",
    "primary_indication": "Pain",
    "indications": "Nefopam Hydrochloride is indicated for the relief of acute pain, including post-operative, dental, musculo-skeletal and acute traumatic pain. It is also indicated in chronic pain like cancer pain.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Nefopam is a non-opioid analgesic and though it acts centrally, its mechanism is not defined. It also exerts antimuscarinic and sympathomimetic actions.",
    "dosage_bn": "Tablet- • Adults: Dosage may range from 30 to 90 mg three times daily depending on response. The recommended starting dosage is 2 tablets three times daily. • Elderly: Elderly patients may require reduced dosage due to slower metabolism. It is strongly recommended that the starting dose does not exceed 1 tablet 3 times daily. Injection- • Adult: 20 mg by IM injection, repeated every 6 hours if necessary. It also be given by slow IV injection in similar dose. • Children: Not recommended for children under the age of 12 years.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Nefopam Hydrochloride is generally well to lerated. However the most common side-effects are nausea, nervousness, dry mouth, lightheadedness and urinary retention.The less common side-effects are vomiting, blurred vision, drowsiness, sweating, insomnia, headache, confusion, hallucinations, tachycardia and aggravation of angina.",
    "precautions_bn": "Nefopam Hydrochloride should be used with caution in patients with glaucoma and with or at risk of urinary retention. Caution should be exercised when Nefopam is administered concurrently with tricyclic antidepressants. Caution should also be exercised in patients with a history of ischaemic heart disease.",
    "pregnancy_category": "Not Classified",
    "brands": "Acupain 30, Acupain Inj, Acuten, Efopam, Neforex, Xripa",
