    "work_bn": "শরীরের অভ্যন্তরীণ বা বাহ্যিক ক্ষতিকর ব্যাকটেরিয়াজনিত জীবাণু ধ্বংস ও মারাত্মক সংক্রমণ প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত অ্যান্টিবায়োটিক। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Tinea corporis (ringworm))",
    "primary_indication": "Tinea corporis (ringworm)",
    "indications": "Naftifine cream is an allylamine antifungal indicated for the treatment of interdigital tinea pedis, tinea cruris, and tinea corporis caused by the organism Trichophyton rubrum",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Although the exact mechanism of action against fungi is not known, naftifine appears to interfere with sterol biosynthesis by inhibiting the enzyme squalene 2,3-epoxidase. This inhibition of enzyme activity results in decreased amounts of sterols, especially ergosterol, and a corresponding accumulation of squalene in the cells.",
    "dosage_bn": "For to pical use only. Naftifine Cream is not for ophthalmic, oral, or intravaginal use. Apply a thin layer of Naftifine Cream once-daily to the affected areas plus a 1/2 inch margin of healthy surrounding skin for 2 weeks",
    "side_effects_bn": "The most common adverse reaction (≥1%) is pruritus.",
