    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Bacterial ear infections)",
    "primary_indication": "Bacterial ear infections",
    "indications": "This ophthalmic ointment or drop is indicated for the to pical treatment of superficial infections of the external eye and its adnexa caused by susceptible bacteria. Such infections encompass conjunctivitis, keratitis and keratoconjunctivitis, blepharitis and blepharoconjunctivitis.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Neomycin, an aminoglyoside with antimicrobial spectrum similar to gentamicin, binds to the 30S subunits of the bacterial ribosome, inhibiting protein synthesis and thereby disrupting DNA synthesis. It is active against many gram-negative aerobes and against some strains of staphylococci. Bacitracin, on the other hand, inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis and is active against many gram-positive bacteria (e.g. staphylococci, streptococci, corynebacteria and Clostridia) and some gram-negative species (e.g. Neisseria and Haemophilus influenzae). They are often found in combinations in to pical preparations as broad spectrum antibacterial agents. Polymyxin B disrupts the bacterial cytoplasmic membrane of mostly gm-ve organisms allowing leakage of intracellular constituents by binding to membrane phospholipids.",
    "dosage_bn": "Eye Drop: 1-2 drops 3-4 times daily. Eye ointment: Apply 1/2 inch ribbon of ointment to conjunctival sac of affected eye(s) q3-4hr for 7-10 days for acute infections",
    "side_effects_bn": "Rash, itching, burning, anaphylactic reactions, swelling, conjunctival erythema.",
    "precautions_bn": "Excessive use of the to pical preparation may lead to substantial systemic absorption which may lead to nephrotoxicity (polymyxin B sulfate) and neurotoxicity (bacitracin). Prolonged use of the antibacterial preparation may cause overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms, including fungi. Pregnancy and lactation.",
