    "id": "med_1618",
    "name_en": "Trimebutine Maleate",
    "generic": "Trimebutine Maleate",
    "category": "digestive",
    "category_bn": "পরিপাক ও এসিডিটি",
    "icon": "🌀",
    "target_organ": "Intestines / অন্ত্র ও বৃহদন্ত্র",
    "organ_key": "intestines",
    "work_bn": "হজম প্রক্রিয়া স্বাভাবিক রাখা, পেটে গ্যাস বা মোচড় দূর করা এবং অন্ত্রের সংক্রমণ বা প্রদাহ উপশমে কার্যকর। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Paralytic ileus and post-operative urinary retention)",
    "primary_indication": "Paralytic ileus and post-operative urinary retention",
    "indications": "Treatment and relief of symptoms associated with irritable bowel syndrome (spastic colon). Postoperative paralytic ileus in order to accelerate the resumption of the intestinal transit following abdominal surgery.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Trimebutine maleate is a noncompetitive spasmolytic agent. It possesses moderate opiate receptor affinity and has marked anti-serotonin activity especially on 'mu' receptors. It induces regulation of spontaneous activity and increases synchronization between electrophysiological spikes and contractions in isolated guinea pig strips of colon and ileum. However, it does not alter normal motility, but regulates abnormal intestinal activity.",
    "dosage_bn": "For adults: 100 mg to 200 mg, 3 times per day before meals.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Trimebutine maleate is generally well to lerated. The infrequently reported adverse effects are as follows: dry mouth, foul taste, diarrhea, dyspepsia, epigastric pain, nausea, constipation, drowsiness, fatigue, dizziness, hot/cold sensations, headache etc.",
    "precautions_bn": "Elderly, pregnancy and lactation",
