    "id": "med_1630",
    "name_en": "Travoprost + Timolol Maleate",
    "generic": "Travoprost + Timolol Maleate",
    "category": "ophthalmic",
    "category_bn": "চোখ ও অপথ্যালমোলজি",
    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Open angle glaucoma)",
    "primary_indication": "Open angle glaucoma",
    "indications": "This Sterile Ophthalmic Solution is indicated for the treatment of elevated intraocular pressure in patients with open angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension who are insufficiently responsive to single therapy with prostaglandin analogue or to pical beta blocker.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Travoprost and Timolol reduce intraocular pressure (IOP) by complementary mechanisms of action. Travoprost is a prostaglandin analogue which reduces IOP by increasing trabecular outflow & uveoscleral outflow. Timolol is a non-selective beta adrenergic receptor blocker that does not have significant intrinsic sympathomimetic, direct myocardial depressant, or local anesthetic (membrane stabilizing) activity. It lowers IOP by decreasing the formation of aqueous humor in the ciliary epithelium.",
    "dosage_bn": "Instill one drop in the conjunctival sac of the affected eye(s) once daily at about the same time each day, preferably in the evening.",
    "side_effects_bn": "No serious adverse reactions are reported. Most frequently reported side effects are ocular hyperemia.",
    "precautions_bn": "For ophthalmic use only. Patients should remove their contact lenses prior to instilling this preparation and should not insert their lenses until 15 minutes after instillation of the preparation.",
