    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Bacterial ocular infections)",
    "primary_indication": "Bacterial ocular infections",
    "indications": "Bacterial ocular infections",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Bacitracin, inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis and is active against many gram-positive bacteria (e.g. staphylococci, streptococci, corynebacteria and clostridia) and some gram-negative species (e.g. Neisseria and Haemophilus influenzae). They are often found in combinations in topical preparations as broad spectrum antibacterial agents. Polymyxin B disrupts the bacterial cytoplasmic membrane of mostly gm-ve organisms allowing leakage of intracellular constituents by binding to membrane phospholipids.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: Ophth Ocular infections; Prevention of ocular infection following surgical procedure: Apply 1/2 inch 3-4 hrly for acute infections or 2-3 times/day for mild-to-moderate infections for 7-10 days. Topical Superficial infections: Apply 1-4 times/day.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Rash, itching, burning, anaphylactic reactions, swelling, conjunctival erythema.",
    "precautions_bn": "Excessive use of the topical preparation may lead to substantial systemic absorption which may lead to nephrotoxicity (polymyxin B sulfate) and neurotoxicity (bacitracin). Prolonged use of the antibacterial preparation may cause overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms, including fungi. Pregnancy and lactation.",
