    "name_en": "Cefepime",
    "generic": "Cefepime",
    "category": "urinary",
    "category_bn": "কিডনি ও মূত্রতন্ত্র",
    "icon": "🫘",
    "target_organ": "Kidneys & Bladder / কিডনি ও মূত্রথলি",
    "organ_key": "kidneys",
    "work_bn": "কিডনি ও মূত্রথলির কার্যক্ষমতা রক্ষা, প্রস্রাবের স্বাভাবিক প্রবাহ নিশ্চিতকরণ এবং প্রোস্টেট উপসর্গ নিরাময়ে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Skin and skin structure infections, Urinary tract infection, Nosocomial pneumonia, Multiple drug resistant pneumonia, Neutropenia)",
    "primary_indication": "Skin and skin structure infections, Urinary tract infection, Nosocomial pneumonia, Multiple drug resistant pneumonia, Neutropenia",
    "indications": "Skin and skin structure infections, Urinary tract infection, Nosocomial pneumonia, Multiple drug resistant pneumonia, Neutropenia",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Cefepime is a 4th generation cephalosporin which inhibits the final transpeptidation step of peptidoglycan synthesis in bacterial cell wall by binding to one or more of the penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs).",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: IV UTI 0.5-1 g 12 hrly for 7-10 days. \\nEmpirical therapy for febrile neutropenia 2 g 8 hrly for 7 days or until resolution of neutropenia. \\nModerate to severe pneumonia 1-2 g 12 hrly for 10 days. \\nComplicated intra-abdominal infections 2 g 12 hrly for 7-10 days. \\nUncomplicated skin and skin structure infections 2 g 12 hrly for 10 days.\\n\\nChild: 2 mth - 16 yr: ?40 kg: 50 mg/kg every 12 hr for 7-10 days for Uncomplicated and Complicated Urinary Tract Infections (including pyelonephritis),\\nUncomplicated Skin and Skin Structure Infections and Pneumonia.. May be given via direct inj over 5 minutes or infuse over 30 minutes.\\n\\nFor empiric therapy for febrile neutropenic patients 2 mth - 16 yr: <40 kg: 50 mg/kg every 8 hr for 7 days or until neutropenia resolves.\\n\\nRenal impairment: Haemodialysis: 1 g on the 1st day of treatment, followed by 0.5 g 24 hrly; dose should be given after haemodialysis on dialysis days and preferably at the same time each day. CAPD: Adult dose 48 hrly.\\n\\nCrCl (ml/min)\\t\\n<10\\t 0.25-0.5 g 24 hrly.\\n11-29\\t0.5-1 g 24 hrly.\\n30-60\\t0.5-2 g 24 hrly.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Positive Coombs' test without haemolysis; rash, pruritus; diarrhoea, nausea, vomiting; fever, headache; pain and erythema at inj site; agranulocytosis; anaphylactic shock; leucopenia; neutropenia; thrombocytopenia.",
    "precautions_bn": "Renal impairment; history of penicillin or cephalosporin allergy; lactation, pregnancy. Caution when used in patients with history of GI diseases, especially colitis. May decrease prothrombin activity; monitor prothrombin time in patients with poor nutritional state, renal or hepatic impairment and those on prolonged treatment. Prolonged treatment may result in overgrowth of nonsusceptible organisms, resulting in superinfection. Consider the possibility of Clostridium difficile associated diarrhoea in patients who present with diarrhoea after treatment. Caution when used in patients with a history of seizures.",
    "pregnancy_category": "B",
    "brands": "Cefa 4 IV/IM, Ceftipime IV/IM, Efepime IV/IM, Forgen IV/IM, Gen 4 IV/IM, Japime IM / IV, Magnova, Maxpime IV/IM",
