    "organ_key": "skin",
    "work_bn": "ত্বকের অ্যালার্জি, চুলকানি, একজিমা, সংক্রমণ ও চর্মরোগের অস্বস্তি নিরাময়ে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Psoriasis, Eczema, Tularaemia, Dermatitis,)",
    "primary_indication": "Psoriasis, Eczema, Tularaemia, Dermatitis,",
    "indications": "Psoriasis, Eczema, Tularaemia, Dermatitis,",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Fluocinolone acetonide is a synthetic fluorinated corticosteroid that is used topically for its anti-inflammatory, anti-pruritic and vasoconstrictive properties. \\nNeomycin is an aminoglycoside antibiotic. It binds to 30S ribosomal subunits of bacterial ribosome thus inhibiting protein synthesis and generating errors in genetic code transcription causing cell death. It acts against many gram-negative aerobes and some gram-positive aerobes. It lacks activity against fungi, viruses and most anaerobic bacteria.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: Topical cream/gel/lotion/oint/scalp lotion: Apply 3-4 times/day.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Dry skin, pruritus, irritation, mild to moderate transient burning/stinging. Local atrophic changes in the skin (prolonged & intensive treatment). Hypercorticism (systemic absorption on prolonged use). Itching, folliculitis, hypertrichoses, acneiform eruptions, hypopigmentation, perioral dermatitis, allergic contact dermatitis, maceration of skin, secondary infections, striae & miliaria. Ototoxicity & nephrotoxicity.\\nProlonged admin causes epidermal thinning, telangiectasia and striae (especially face and flexures). Application on eyelid and surrounding skin can cause raised intraocular pressure, cataracts, glaucoma, corneal ulcers and raised intracranial pressure. Systemic absorption with adrenal suppression may be seen when applied over large areas, when skin is broken or under occlusive dressing.",
    "precautions_bn": "Children, elderly, hepatic failure. Prolonged use on the face; contact with eyes. Pregnancy, lactation.",
    "pregnancy_category": "C",
