    "primary_indication": "Dermatophytosis",
    "indications": "Dermatophytosis",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Griseofulvin is a fungistatic antibiotic that inhibits fungal cell division at metaphase and binds to human keratin making it resistant to fungal infections. It has activity against common dermatophytes including epidermophyton, Microsporum, or Trichophyton spp.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: PO 0.5-1 g/day. Hair and skin infecions: 2-8 wk. Fingernail infections: 6 mth. Toenail infections: 12 mth or more.\\n\\nChild: 10 mg/kg daily.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Oral thrush; GI distress, taste perversion; dizziness, confusion, headache, depression, insomnia, fatigue; peripheral neuritis, photosensitivity; skin rashes, urticaria, erythema multiforme; leucopenia, proteinuria.\\nPotentially Fatal: Hepatotoxicity; angioedema.",
    "precautions_bn": "Lactation; may impair ability to drive or operate machinery; avoid exposure to intense sunlight or artificial light. Regular monitoring of the renal, hepatic and blood tests should be done.",
