    "work_bn": "চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ অনুযায়ী নিম্নলিখিত সমস্যার চিকিৎসায় কার্যকর: Chronic myeloid leukaemia, Acute lymphoblastic leukaemia, Myelodysplastic disease, Hypereosinophilic syndrome, Mastocytosis, Dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans, Malignant gastrointestinal stromal tumours।",
    "primary_indication": "Chronic myeloid leukaemia, Acute lymphoblastic leukaemia, Myelodysplastic disease, Hypereosinophilic syndrome, Mastocytosis, Dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans, Malignant gastrointestinal stromal tumours",
    "indications": "Chronic myeloid leukaemia, Acute lymphoblastic leukaemia, Myelodysplastic disease, Hypereosinophilic syndrome, Mastocytosis, Dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans, Malignant gastrointestinal stromal tumours",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Imatinib, is a tyrosine kinase inhibitor that inhibits the BCR-ABL tyrosine kinase created by the Philadelphia chromosome abnormality in chronic myeloid leukaemia (CML). It blocks proliferation and induces apoptosis in BCR-ABL positive cell lines, as well as fresh leukaemic cells from Philadelphia chromosome positive CML. Imatinib also inhibits receptor kinases for platelet-derived growth factor (PDGF) and stem cell factor (SCF), c-kit, PDGF- and SCF-mediated cellular events.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: PO Chronic myeloid leukaemia Chronic phase: 400 mg/day, up to 600 mg/day. Blast crisis or aceelerated phase: 600 mg/day, up to 400 mg twice daily if needed. \\n\\nAcute lymphoblastic leukaemia; Monotherapy in relapsed or refractory acute lymphoblastic leukaemia 600 mg/day w/ induction, maintenance or consolidation therapy. \\n\\nHypereosinophilic syndrome; Myelodysplastic disease 400 mg/day. Unresectable, metastatic GI stromal tumours 400 or 600 mg/day. \\n\\nMastocytosis 400 mg/day. Start w/ 100 mg/day if there is associated eosinophilia. Dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans 400 mg twice daily.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Fluid retention/oedema, nausea and vomiting, muscle cramps, musculoskeletal pain, diarrhoea, rash. Fatigue, asthenia, headache, dizziness, insomnia, depression, anxiety, joint pain, arthralgia, myalgia, back pain, abdominal pain, flatulence, dyspepsia, loose stools, anorexia, constipation, taste disturbance, nasopharyngitis, cough, pharyngolaryngeal pain, pharyngitis, sinusitis, upper respiratory tract infection, pneumonia, influenza, dyspnoea, haemorrhage, pyrexia, increased wt, night sweats, rigors, hepatotoxi",
    "precautions_bn": "Cardiac disease or increased risk for CHF. Monitor for signs of severe fluid retention. Monitor CBC regularly. Renal and hepatic impairment. Monitor LFTs. Pregnancy.",
    "pregnancy_category": "D",
