    "primary_indication": "Wound and ulcer cleansing, Superficial wounds",
    "indications": "Wound and ulcer cleansing, Superficial wounds",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Topical iodine acts as a local irritant and as a germicide active against gram-positive and gram-negative bacteria, fungi, trichomonas, cysts, viruses and some spores.",
    "dosage_bn": "Gargle and Mouth-Wash: Adults and children over 6 years, gargle with up to 10 ml undiluted or diluted with an equal quantity of warm water for up to 30 seconds, up to 4 times daily for up to 14 days. \\n\\nSolution: Apply the full strength as often as required as a paint or wet soak. For minor wounds and infection apply directly to the affected area. The site may be covered with gauze or adhesive bandage. Ointment: Apply ointment directly to the affected area after being cleaned and dried. May be covered with a dressing or bandage.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Idiosyncratic mucosal irritation and hypersensitivity reactions rarely, may interfere with thyroid-function tests.",
