    "organ_key": "lungs",
    "work_bn": "শ্বাসনালী উন্মুক্ত রাখা, কাশি উপশম, ফুসফুসের প্রদাহ রোধ এবং হাঁপানি বা শ্বাসকষ্টের সমস্যা প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Asthma, Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease)",
    "primary_indication": "Asthma, Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease",
    "indications": "Asthma, Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Ipratropium bromide is an anticholinergic agent that inhibits vagally-mediated reflexes by antagonising the action of acetylcholine. It prevents the increases in intracellular concentration of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cyclic GMP) which are brought about by interaction of acetylcholine with the muscarinic receptors on bronchial smooth muscle. Salbutamol is a direct-acting beta 2-adrenergic agent. It acts on the airway smooth muscle resulting in bronchodilation.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: Inhalation Per inhalation contains ipratropium bromide 18 mcg and salbutamol sulfate 103 mcg: 2 inhalations 4 times/day. Max: 12 inhalations/24 hr. \\n\\nFor nebulising solution (each 3 ml contains ipratropium bromide 0.5 mg and salbutamol base 2.5 mg): Initially, 3 ml every 6 hr. Max: 3 ml every 4 hr.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Bronchitis, respiratory tract infections. Chest pain, arrhythmia, oedema, hypertension, hypokalaemia, palpitation, tachycardia. Headache, dizziness, fatigue, insomnia, tremor, nervousness. GI symptoms e.g. nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, dyspepsia and constipation.\\nPotentially Fatal: Anaphylactic reactions such as angioedema of tongue, lips or face and laryngospasm.",
    "precautions_bn": "May cause paradoxical bronchospasm. Caution when used in patients who are sensitive to sympathomimetic agents. Caution when used in patients with CV disease as ?-agonists may increase BP, heart rate and risk of arrhythmias. Monitor blood glucose in diabetics. Monitor serum potassium levels especially in patients who are on concurrent treatment with xanthine derivatives, steroids or diuretics. Caution when used in patients with narrow angle glaucoma, hyperthyroidism, prostatic hyperplasia, bladder neck obstruction, seizure disorders, renal or hepatic impairment. Safety and efficacy have not been established in children <12 yr. Increased risk of GI motility disturbance in patients with cystic fibrosis. Pregnancy and lactation.",
    "pregnancy_category": "C",
    "brands": "Combair HFA, Combair HFA Refill, Combair Resp Sol, Combiver-AF, Ipralin HFA, Iprasol, Iprasol HFA, Salpium",
