    "target_organ": "Lungs / ফুসফুস ও শ্বাসতন্ত্র",
    "organ_key": "lungs",
    "work_bn": "শ্বাসনালী উন্মুক্ত রাখা, কাশি উপশম, ফুসফুসের প্রদাহ রোধ এবং হাঁপানি বা শ্বাসকষ্টের সমস্যা প্রতিরোধে ব্যবহৃত হয়। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Pain, MI, Unstable angina, Intractable cough, Acute pulmonary oedema, Analgesia during labour)",
    "primary_indication": "Pain, MI, Unstable angina, Intractable cough, Acute pulmonary oedema, Analgesia during labour",
    "indications": "Pain, MI, Unstable angina, Intractable cough, Acute pulmonary oedema, Analgesia during labour",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Morphine is a phenanthrene derivative which acts mainly on the CNS and smooth muscles. It binds to opiate receptors in the CNS altering pain perception and response. Analgesia, euphoria and dependence are thought to be due to its action at the mu-1 receptors while resp depression and inhibition of intestinal movements are due to action at the mu-2 receptors. Spinal analgesia is mediated by morphine agonist action at the K receptor.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: PO Pain relief 5-20 mg 4 hrly. Intractable cough associated w/ lung cancer As oral soln: Initial: 5 mg 4 hrly. \\n\\nIV Pain associated w/ MI 10 mg, then a further dose of 5-10 mg if needed. \\nAcute pulmonary oedema 5-10 mg. Unstable angina unresponsive to anti-ischaemic therapy 2-5 mg repeated every 5-30 mins as needed. Acute pain Initial: 2.5 mg 4 hrly, adjust according to response. \\n\\nIM/SC Acute pain 10 mg 4 hrly, adjust according to response. Premed in surgical procedures Up to 10 mg 60-90 mins pre-op. Analgesia during labour 10 mg. Intrathecal Moderate to severe pain 0.2-1 mg on a single occasion. Intraspinal Moderate to severe pain Initial: 5 mg epidural inj; after 1 hr, additional doses of 1-2 mg may be given if needed. Total dose: 10 mg/24 hr.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Convulsions; nausea, vomiting, dry mouth, constipation; urinary retention; headache, vertigo; palpitations; hypothermia; pruritus, urticaria; tachycardia, bradycardia; blurred vision; miosis; dependency; drowsiness; lightheadedness; dizziness; sweating; dysphoria; euphoria.\\nPotentially Fatal: Respiratory depression; circulatory failure; hypotension; deepening coma; anaphylactic reactions.",
    "precautions_bn": "Elderly; hypothyroidism; renal and liver disease; head injury, intracranial lesions; hypotension, circulatory shock; adrenocortical insufficiency; asthma; prostatic hyperplasia; inflammatory or obstructive bowel disease; myasthaenia gravis; infants <3 mth; pregnancy, lactation; hypovolaemia, biliary tract disorders.",
    "pregnancy_category": "D",
    "brands": "G Morphine, G Morphine SR, Morphin-R, Morphine, MSL-10",
