    "primary_indication": "Dry mouth, Sjogren's syndrome",
    "indications": "Dry mouth, Sjogren's syndrome",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Pilocarpine is a tertiary parasympathomimetic that directly stimulates cholinergic receptors in the eyes causing pupillary constriction, spasm of accommodation and a transient rise in IOP followed by a fall.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: PO Dry mouth after radiotherapy for malignant neoplasms of the head and neck Initial: 5 mg 3 times/day. Increase gradually after 4 wk if needed. Max: 10 mg 3 times/day. \\n\\nSjoren's syndrome 5 mg 4 times/day. Max: 30 mg/day. Stop treatment if no improvement after 3 mth.",
