    "work_bn": "চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ অনুযায়ী নিম্নলিখিত সমস্যার চিকিৎসায় কার্যকর: Anogenital warts।",
    "primary_indication": "Anogenital warts",
    "indications": "Anogenital warts",
    "how_it_works_bn": "The mechanism of action of podophyllo toxin is based on inhibiting the polymerization of tubulin and arresting the cell cycle in the metaphase.",
    "dosage_bn": "Topical/Cutaneous\\nAnogenital warts\\nAdult: On a wkly basis, apply 15% (Indian podophyllum) or up to 25% solution (American podophyllum) on the warts, leave for 1-6 hr then wash off. If there is no improvement after 6 wk, stop treatment. Alternatively, apply 0.5% alcoholic gel or 0.15% cream bid for 3 days but do not wash off. Repeat wkly for up to 5 wk.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Irritating to the eyes and mucous membranes; GI disturbances; thrombocytopenia, leucopenia; renal failure; hepatotoxicity; CNS effects; EEG changes; peripheral and autonomic neuropathies; local reactions.",
    "precautions_bn": "\\tAvoid excessive application. Avoid contact with eyes and inflamed skin. Not to be used on cervical or urethral warts.",
