    "target_organ": "Body Surface (Skin) / ত্বক",
    "organ_key": "skin",
    "work_bn": "ত্বকের অ্যালার্জি, চুলকানি, একজিমা, সংক্রমণ ও চর্মরোগের অস্বস্তি নিরাময়ে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Acne, Stable plaque psoriasis, Photo aging)",
    "primary_indication": "Acne, Stable plaque psoriasis, Photo aging",
    "indications": "Acne, Stable plaque psoriasis, Photo aging",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Tazarotene is a synthetic acetylenic retinoid, that is applied topically. It is de-esterified in the skin to its active form, tazarotenic acid, which affects cell proliferation and differentiation by modulating gene expression in acne and psoriasis.",
    "dosage_bn": "For psoriasis: Apply once daily in the evening usually for up to twelve weeks. Use and dose must be determined by the doctor of children upto 12 years of age.\\nFor acne: Cleanse the face gently. After the skin is dry, apply a thin layer of Tazarotene cream once per day, in the evening, to the skin areas where acne lesions appear. Use enough to cover the entire affeted area.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Generally Tazarotene cream is well-tolerated .The most frequent adverse events related to treatment with Tazarotene are skin-related as for example pruritus, erythema, burning, irritation, desquamation, stinging, contact dermatitis, dermatitis, eczema, worsening of psoriasis, skin pain, rash, hypertriglyceridemia, dry skin, skin inflammation, and peripheral edema.",
    "precautions_bn": "Tazarotene cream should be applied only to the affected areas. It is for external use only. Avoid contact with eyes, eyelids, and mouth. If contact with eyes occurs, rinse thoroughly with water.\\nRetinoid should not be used on eczematous skin, as they may cause severe irritation.\\nBecause of heightened burning susceptibility, exposure to sunlight (including sunlamps) should be avoided unless deemed medically necessary and in such cases, exposure should be minimized during the use of Tazarotene cream. Tazarotene cream should be administered with caution if the patient is also taking drugs known to be photosensitizers (e.g., thiazides, tetracyclines, fluoroquinolones, phenothiazines, sulfonamides) because of the increased possibility of augmented photosensitivity.",
    "pregnancy_category": "X",
    "brands": "Soritene, Tazoskin",
