    "work_bn": "চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ অনুযায়ী নিম্নলিখিত সমস্যার চিকিৎসায় কার্যকর: Lymphoma, Squamous cell or Testicular tumours, Malignant effusions।",
    "primary_indication": "Lymphoma, Squamous cell or Testicular tumours, Malignant effusions",
    "indications": "Lymphoma, Squamous cell or Testicular tumours, Malignant effusions",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Bleomycin causes breakage of single- and double- stranded DNA by binding to DNA and inhibiting DNA synthesis. To a lesser extent, it also inhibits RNA and protein synthesis. It causes very little bone marrow suppression.",
    "dosage_bn": "Parenteral\\nSquamous cell or testicular tumours\\nAdult: 15,000 IU 3 times a wk or 30,000 IU twice a wk IM/IV, repeated at usual intervals of 3-4 wk up to a total cumulative dose of 500,000 IU.\\nElderly: Dose reduction is necessary.\\nIntramuscular\\nLymphoma\\nAdult: 15,000 IU once or twice a wk, up to a total cumulative dose of 225,000 IU.\\nElderly: Dose reduction is necessary.\\nInjection\\nMalignant effusions\\nAdult: 60,000 IU in 100 ml of 0.9% sodium chloride instilled into the affected serous cavity, may be repeated up to a total cumulative dose of 500,000 IU.\\nElderly: Dose reduction is necessary.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Fever, thrombophloebitis (inj). Acute anaphylactoid reactions, hyperpyrexia. Rash, erythema, pruritus, vesiculation, hyperkeratosis, nail changes, alopecia, hyperpigmentation, striae, stomatitis.\\nPotentially Fatal: Pulmonary toxicity, interstitial pneumonitis, fibrosis, cardiorespiratory collapse in patients with lymphoma.",
    "precautions_bn": "Pulmonary infection, preexisting pulmonary function impairment, renal impairment. Patients who received radiotherapy, particularly to the thorax. Regular chest x-rays should be done. Elderly. Discontinue treatment if chest x-rays show infiltrates or breathlessness occurs.",
    "pregnancy_category": "D",
