    "primary_indication": "Anovulatory infertility, Adjunct to IVF procedures and other assisted conception techniques",
    "indications": "Anovulatory infertility, Adjunct to IVF procedures and other assisted conception techniques",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Choriogonadotropin alfa is a recombinant form of chorionic gonadotrophin. Its effects mimic those of leuteinizing hormone, which triggers ovulation and formation of the corpus luteum in women and stimulates the production of testosterone by the testes in men.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: SC Anovulatory infertility; Adjunct to IVF procedures and other assisted conception techniques 250 mcg as a single dose when optimal stimulation of follicular growth in achieved.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Nausa, vomiting, abdominal pain; headache, tiredness; Inj site reactions; ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome; rarely diarrhoea, depression, irritability, breast pain. Ectopic pregnancy, ovarian torsion and other complications in some patients after hCG administration.",
    "precautions_bn": "Asthma, epilepsy, migraine, CV disorders, renal disorders; infertility caused by hyperprolactinaemia, pituitary or hypothalamic tumors; clinically significant systemic diseases where pregnancy could exacerbate the condition. Monitor carefully estradiol levels and ovarian response based on ultrasound prior to and during stimulation therapy. Multiple pregnancy.",
