    "icon": "🩺",
    "target_organ": "General Physiology / সার্বিক শারীরবৃত্ত",
    "organ_key": "general",
    "work_bn": "চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ অনুযায়ী নিম্নলিখিত সমস্যার চিকিৎসায় কার্যকর: Contraception।",
    "primary_indication": "Contraception",
    "indications": "Contraception",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Etonogestrel is the active metabolite of desogestrel. It prevents pregnancy by suppressing ovulation, increasing viscosity of cervical mucous and inhibiting endometrial proliferation.",
    "dosage_bn": "Adult: Vag Per vag ring delivers etonorgestrel 120 mcg and ethinylestradiol 15 mcg daily. Insert 1 ring into the vagina on the 1st day of menstruation. Leave the ring in place for 3 wk, then allow for 1 wk break. Insert a new ring 1 wk after removal of the previous ring. Subdermal Per implant contains 68 mg of etonorgestrel: Insert 1 implant during the 1st 5 days of menstruation. Remove no later than 3 yr after date of insertion.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Menstrual irregularities; nausea, vomiting, headache, dizziness, breast discomfort, gynaecomastia, depression, skin disorders, disturbance of appetite, wt changes, fluid retention, oedema, changes in libido, cholestatic jaundice, hair loss or hirsutism.",
    "precautions_bn": "Heart disease, sex-steroid dependent cancer, history of ectopic pregnancy, malabsorption syndromes, functional ovarian cysts, recurrent cholestatic jaundice, history of jaundice in pregnancy; history of pruritus during pregnancy or of deterioration of otosclerosis; disturbances of lipid metabolism; history of CV or renal impairment, DM, asthma, epilepsy, migraine, depression; lactation. May develop bleeding irregularities.",
    "pregnancy_category": "Not Classified",
