    "id": "med_2475",
    "name_en": "Prednisolone Acetate + Neomycin Sulphate E/E prep",
    "generic": "Prednisolone Acetate + Neomycin Sulphate E/E prep",
    "category": "ophthalmic",
    "category_bn": "চোখ ও অপথ্যালমোলজি",
    "icon": "👁️",
    "target_organ": "Eyes / চোখ",
    "organ_key": "eyes_ears",
    "work_bn": "চোখের সংক্রমণ, চুলকানি, অতিরিক্ত শুষ্কতা দূর এবং দৃষ্টিশক্তি সুরক্ষা ও চোখের উচ্চচাপ কমাতে নির্দেশিত। (মূল নির্দেশিকা: Allergic and inflammatory conditions of the eye & ear.)",
    "primary_indication": "Allergic and inflammatory conditions of the eye & ear.",
    "indications": "Allergic and inflammatory conditions of the eye & ear.",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Prednisolone decreases inflammation by inhibition of migration of polymorphonuclear leukocytes and reversal of increased capillary permeability. It suppresses the immune system by reducing the activity and production of the lymphocytes and eosinophils.\\n\\nNeomycin is an aminoglycoside antibiotic. It binds to 30S ribosomal subunits of bacterial ribosome thus inhibiting protein synthesis and generating errors in genetic code transcription causing cell death. It acts against many gram-negative aerobes and some gram-positive aerobes. It lacks activity against fungi, viruses and most anaerobic bacteria.",
    "dosage_bn": "Conjunctivitis\\nAdult & Child: Instill 1-2 drops into the affected eye(s) 2-4 times daily. \\nOtic/Aural\\nAllergic and inflammatory conditions of the ear\\nAdult & Child:1-2 drops into the affected ear 3-4 times daily. \\n",
    "side_effects_bn": "Ophthalmic: Raised IOP and reduced visual function.\\nEar: Discomfort & pain in ear.\\n",
    "precautions_bn": "Patients with hypothyroidism, cirrhosis, ulcerative colitis, CHF, convulsive disorders, thrombophlebitis, peptic ulcer, elderly. DM, hypertension, psychological disturbances, osteoporosis; pregnancy, lactation. Adrenal suppression and infection. May cause irreversible growth retardation, glaucoma, corneal perforation. Topical: Broken or infected skin. Not to be applied over large areas under occlusive dressings.",
    "pregnancy_category": "C+D",
