    "id": "med_2487",
    "name_en": "Salicylic Acid 16.7% + Lactic Acid 16.7%",
    "generic": "Salicylic Acid 16.7% + Lactic Acid 16.7%",
    "category": "other",
    "category_bn": "অন্যান্য বিশেষ ওষুধ",
    "icon": "🩺",
    "target_organ": "General Physiology / সার্বিক শারীরবৃত্ত",
    "organ_key": "general",
    "work_bn": "চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ অনুযায়ী নিম্নলিখিত সমস্যার চিকিৎসায় কার্যকর: Warts।",
    "primary_indication": "Warts",
    "indications": "Warts",
    "how_it_works_bn": "Salicylic acid has a potent keratolytic action and a slight antiseptic action when applied topically. It softens and destroys the stratum corneum by increasing endogenous hydration which causes the horny layer of the skin to swell, soften, and then desquamate. At high concentrations, salicylic acid has a caustic effect. It also possesses weak antifungal and antibacterial activity.\\n\\nIt is commonly used for lubricating and moisturising skin, thus relieving dryness and itch.",
    "dosage_bn": "i. Wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water before and after using this medication.ii. Soak the wart in hot water for at least five minutes.iii. Use an emery board or pumice stone to rub off the dead skin in the affected area (avoid sharing this board/ stone with others).iv. Dry the area thoroughly.v. Use the applicator to apply 2 to 4 drops of the medication directly to the wart once a day. Note: Allow each drop to dry before the next is applied. DO NOT apply the medication to surrounding healthy skin.vi. Cover the treated area with a plaster or adhesive tape.",
    "side_effects_bn": "Possible side effects:\\nStinging, burning, or irritation of the skin\\nItching\\nProlonged use over a large skin area may cause salicylate toxicity. \\nRinging sound in the ears (tinnitus)\\nDiarrhoea\\nVomiting",
    "precautions_bn": "\\tNot for prolonged use in high concentrations and on large areas of the body. Impaired peripheral circulation or diabetes. Avoid broken skin, mouth, eyes, mucous membranes and anogenital region.\\n\\n",
    "pregnancy_category": "Not Classified",
